        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Back pain, reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Low thoracic/upper lumbar ache for approximately 3 weeks, worse at the end of the day and with prolonged standing. Patient reports no trauma, radiation to the legs, paraesthesia, weakness, saddle anaesthesia, or bowel or bladder symptoms. Intermittent Panadol provides partial relief."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shoulder pain, reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Insidious right shoulder pain for approximately 3–4 months, anterolateral shoulder radiating to the lateral upper arm. Worse with overhead activity, reaching into cupboards, and lying on the right side; wakes him. Difficulty lifting a kettle with the right arm. Patient reports no neck pain or distal paraesthesia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
